<title>USA: UPS pilots union votes stike authorization.</title>
<headline>UPS pilots union votes stike authorization.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Independent Pilots Association said Tuesday that 94 percent of the nearly 2,000 pilots employed by United Parcel Service voted to authorize a strike if an agreement is not soon reached with the big carrier.</p>
<p>A strike count Monday revealed that all but 28 of the 1,874 pilots who cast ballots voted in favor of authorizing a strike.  </p>
<p>The pilots said the strike vote comes a month after UPS &quot;suddenly&quot; withdrew its previous contract offer from the bargaining table and requested intervention by federal mediators.</p>
<p>UPS and IPA have been negotiating since 1995. The pilots are scheduled to hold a conference call with reporters later Tuesday.</p>
</text>
